/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:9:#  File Description:                                                      #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:10:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:11:#  This file contains the rules used by UDEV when creating entries for    #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:12:#  Digilent USB devices. In order for Digilent's shared libraries and     #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:13:#  applications to access these devices without root privalages it is     #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:14:#  necessary for UDEV to create entries for which all users have read     #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:15:#  and write permission.                                                  #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:16:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:17:#  Usage:                                                                 #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:18:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:19:#  Copy this file to "/etc/udev/rules.d/" and execute                     #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:20:#  "/sbin/udevcontrol reload_rules" as root. This only needs to be done   #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:21:#  immediately after installation. Each time you reboot your system the   #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:22:#  rules are automatically loaded by UDEV.                                #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:23:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:24:###########################################################################
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:25:#  Revision History:                                                      #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:26:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:27:#  04/15/2010(MTA): created                                               #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:28:#  02/28/2011(MTA): modified to support FTDI based devices                #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:29:#  07/10/2012(MTA): modified to work with UDEV versions 098 or newer      #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:30:#  04/19/2013(MTA): modified mode assignment to use ":=" insetead of "="  #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:31:#       so that our permission settings can't be overwritten by other     #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:32:#       rules files                                                       #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:33:#  07/28/2014(MTA): changed default application path                      #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:34:#                                                                         #
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:35:###########################################################################
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:36:
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:37:# Create "/dev" entries for Digilent device's with read and write
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:38:# permission granted to all users.
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:39:ATTR{idVendor}=="1443", MODE:="666"
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:40:ACTION=="add", ATTR{idVendor}=="0403", ATTR{manufacturer}=="Digilent", MODE:="666"
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:41:
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:42:# The following rules (if present) cause UDEV to ignore all UEVENTS for
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:43:# which the subsystem is "usb_endpoint" and the action is "add" or
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:44:# "remove". These rules are necessary to work around what appears to be a
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:45:# bug in the Kernel used by Red Hat Enterprise Linux 5/CentOS 5. The Kernel
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:46:# sends UEVENTS to remove and then add entries for the endpoints of a USB
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:47:# device in "/dev" each time a process releases an interface. This occurs
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:48:# each time a data transaction occurs. When an FPGA is configured or flash
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:49:# device is written a large number of transactions take place. If the
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:50:# following lines are commented out then UDEV will be overloaded for a long
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:51:# period of time while it tries to process the massive number of UEVENTS it
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:52:# receives from the kernel. Please note that this work around only applies
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:53:# to systems running RHEL5 or CentOS 5 and as a result the rules will only
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-digilent-usb.rules:54:# be present on those systems.
