/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:30:# version 0001
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:31:# Create "/dev" entries for Xilinx device's with read and write
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:32:# permission granted to all users.
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:33:ACTION=="add", ATTR{idVendor}=="0403", ATTR{manufacturer}=="Xilinx", MODE:="666"
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:34:
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:35:# The following rules (if present) cause UDEV to ignore all UEVENTS for
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:36:# which the subsystem is "usb_endpoint" and the action is "add" or
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:37:# "remove". These rules are necessary to work around what appears to be a
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:38:# bug in the Kernel used by Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6/CentOS 5. The Kernel
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:39:# sends UEVENTS to remove and then add entries for the endpoints of a USB
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:40:# device in "/dev" each time a process releases an interface. This occurs
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:41:# each time a data transaction occurs. When an FPGA is configured or flash
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:42:# device is written a large number of transactions take place. If the
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:43:# following lines are commented out then UDEV will be overloaded for a long
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:44:# period of time while it tries to process the massive number of UEVENTS it
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:45:# receives from the kernel. Please note that this work around only applies
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:46:# to systems running RHEL6 or CentOS 5 and as a result the rules will only
/tools/Xilinx/Vivado/2023.1/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers/52-xilinx-ftdi-usb.rules:47:# be present on those systems.
